INT. ROLLER RINK SNACK BAR - CLOSING TIME

A cramped counter under a flickering neon sign. The popcorn machine ticks as it cools. Mirror-ball light crawls over a floor of scuffed maple. Rental skates hang in crooked rows.

IMANI VOSS (30s, braids pinned up, rink-staff polo two sizes big) wipes the counter in slow circles. She has been wiping the same spot for a while.

TEODOR LIND (30s, rangy, wool coat, skate laces knotted round one wrist) stands at the far end holding a paper boat of cold fries.

IMANI
We close in five.

TEODOR
I know. I'm eating.

Imani nods. Keeps wiping.

GRANDMA PEARL (70s, tiny, sequined cardigan, terrifyingly good on skates) glides up to the counter and raps it twice with a knuckle.

PEARL
Two cocoas. One for me, one for the man who's about to say something.

TEODOR
I wasn't going to.

PEARL
That's what I'm afraid of.

DESMOND "DEZ" ACHTERBERG (20s, gangly, headset askew) leans out of the DJ booth and cups a hand to his mouth.

DEZ
Last song! Anybody left, last song!

CLEO (teens, braces, rental skates on the wrong feet) wobbles in from the rink, grabs the counter, and lets go of it again at once.

Imani and Teodor both reach to steady her. Their hands meet on Cleo's sleeve. Both pull back. Cleo sits down on the floor.

CLEO
I'm fine.

IMANI
You're on the floor.

CLEO
Fine on the floor.

Pearl slides two cocoas across. Teodor takes his and does not drink it.

TEODOR
I drove four hours.

IMANI
Nobody asked you to.

TEODOR
You did. In March.

IMANI
In March I was talking.

Pearl turns her cocoa a quarter turn on the counter, in no hurry.

PEARL
(to Cleo)
Up, sweetheart. This part's boring.

Cleo scrambles up. Pearl steers her toward the rink by the elbow, and the two of them roll away.

Dez cuts the music. The room hums. The mirror ball keeps turning without a song.

IMANI
Teo.

TEODOR
Imani.

They speak at the same moment.

IMANI
I should have called.

TEODOR ^
I should have stayed.

Neither laughs. Imani folds the rag into a square.

IMANI
It's a long drive back.

TEODOR
It is.

He sets the fries down and picks them up again. Imani reaches under the counter and hands him a napkin.

TEODOR (CONT'D)
Thanks.

IMANI
Go on. I have to lock up.

He nods. At the door he stops, and she does not look up. Dez flips the house lights on, and the whole rink goes flat and bright.

CLEO (O.S.)
Are we allowed to keep the skates?

DEZ
No!

Teodor pushes the door open and the cold comes in.
